.TH FWRITE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fwrite \- write items to a Crunch file stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fwrite(const void* " buffer ", size_t " size ", size_t " count ", struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes up to
.I count
items of
.I size
bytes from the buffer. A partial final item may be written but does not count
as a complete item. A zero size or count returns zero without I/O.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of complete items written. On error the stream error
indicator is set and
.B errno
is set. A null nonempty buffer or stream sets
.BR EINVAL ;
a size/count product exceeding the supported signed 64-bit byte range sets
.BR EOVERFLOW .
.SH NOTES
I/O is unbuffered; interrupted writes report an error.
Use
.BR ferror (3crunch)
to inspect the stream error indicator.
Crunch streams are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch),
.BR fseek (3crunch),
.BR fread (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch)
